# Code Style

## Formatting
- Run the project formatter (`dart format`) and keep its output; don't hand-tweak layout.
- Use consistent indentation; never mix tabs and spaces in one file.
- Remove trailing whitespace and leave a single newline at end of file.

## Naming
- `lowerCamelCase` for variables/functions, `UpperCamelCase` for classes/widgets/enums, `lowercase_with_underscores` for file names.
- Use descriptive names; avoid abbreviations like `tmp`, `d`, `val2`.
- Booleans read as questions: `isLoading`, `hasAccess`, `canEdit`.

## Functions & files
- Keep functions/widgets small and single-purpose; extract widgets when build methods grow.
- Prefer early returns over deep nesting.
- One main concern per file; split when a file gets large.

## Cleanliness
- No dead code, commented-out blocks, or stray `print` in commits.
- Remove unused imports and variables.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*. Don't narrate obvious code.

## Imports
- Group imports: Dart/Flutter SDK first, then packages, then local files.
- Avoid wildcard imports; import only what's used.

